  "motion": {
    "frames": 120,
    "note": "giant venomous centipede reared to strike, menacing not graceful: crouched low on its legs, torso leaning in, the neck in an S and the head held over it aimed down at prey. Driver: a slow lateral wave travels up the segmented body from the hips through the spine to the neck, with a heave riding along it; the legs ripple back to front, each a quarter loop after the one behind (planted feet, the knees take it); the head sways against the neck so it stays aimed, poised; the neck plates and waist plates ripple a beat later; the antennae (head) and the tail horns twitch in short decaying flicks",
